    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The test passes (BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required validating the E.164 telephone's **national-number length against its country code**. The existing `Telephones.toE164` only enforced a generic \"8\u201315 digits after the `+`\" range \u2014 so a `+61` number with the wrong national length (e.g. 7 or 10 national digits) would have been wrongly accepted.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Telephones.java`:\n\n- Added a `NATIONAL_DIGITS` map (`+61` \u2192 9, `+1` \u2192 10), ordered longest-prefix-first so a `+61` number is tested against `+61` before the shorter `+1`.\n- After the existing general E.164 check, the code now finds the matching country code, counts the national digits (total length minus the country-code length), and throws the checked `InvalidTelephoneException` when it isn't exactly what that country requires. Unrecognised country codes remain bound only by the general 8\u201315 range.\n- Updated the class Javadoc to document the per-country rule.\n\nThe existing `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` already maps that exception to **400 Bad Request**, and the escalation YAML wires it up \u2014 so no other files needed touching.\n\nVerification of the two paths:\n- Reject: `\"+61 123\"` \u2192 normalizes to `+61123` (3 national digits, \u2260 9) \u2192 400. \u2713 (the new test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength`)\n- Accept: the happy-path `uniqueTelephone()` (`04XXXXXXXX`) drops the leading `0` \u2192 9 national digits under `+61` \u2192 still valid. \u2713\n\n`./mvnw -Dtest=AcceptanceTest test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test green.\n\nOne thing worth flagging (I did **not** change it, since it's outside this spec and untested): the `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}` path via `ApplyOwner` copies the telephone straight onto the entity without calling `Telephones.toE164`, so updates bypass this validation entirely. Let me know if you'd like that path normalized/validated too.",
